        "title": "Priority Order",
        "content": "| Priority | File | Tests to add | Impact |\n|----------|------|-------------|--------|\n| **1** | `test_llm_client.py` | JSON parsing, malformed, truncated, API error | Every agent depends on this |\n| **2** | `test_specialist_agent.py` | Core pipeline, fetch failure, LLM failure | Primary query workflow |\n| **3** | `test_orchestrator_agent.py` | Routing, synthesis, deduplication, conflicts | End-to-end correctness |\n| **4** | `test_fetch_engine.py` | Timeout fallback, partial batch failure, rate limiting | Reliability |\n| **5** | `test_fetch_cache.py` | TTL expiry, stale fallback, domain TTLs | Resilience |\n| **6** | `test_database.py` | All CRUD methods, cache, feedback | Data integrity |\n| **7** | `test_api_routes.py` | Validation, 404s, edge cases | API contract |\n| **8** | `test_websocket.py` | Disconnect, malformed input | Real-time safety |\n| **9** | `test_config.py` | Missing file, bad YAML, env overrides | Startup safety |\n\nImplementing Tier 1–3 would bring coverage from ~9.5% to approximately 60–70% and cover every critical failure mode in production.",
